## 4. Direct quotes and data points usable verbatim

1. **On United's role in the Dulles program (attributable, on the record):** "We designed it by and large. We're excited about it." — United CEO Scott Kirby on the $22.5B Dulles revitalization [Source: https://byerussell.substack.com/p/uniteds-vision-for-dulles-is-a-go]. *Use:* establishes that any MWAA standard applied to United premises at IAD is negotiated with United, not imposed on it.

2. **On the CPE trajectory (numerical, sourced):** MWAA's 2025 Official Statement projected IAD CPE rising to **$20.71 by 2030**; a May 2026 airline briefing on the revised $22.5B program projected IAD CPE reaching **$90.64 by 2035**, a figure United's CEO has publicly disputed on volume-dilution grounds [Sources: https://dwuconsulting.com/dwu-ai/dulles-rfi-analysis and https://www.bondbuyer.com/news/dulles-expansion-raising-questions and https://byerussell.substack.com/p/uniteds-vision-for-dulles-is-a-go]. *Use:* any addition to program scope — including a quiet-by-design standard — is measured against this trajectory, not against a $12.77 current baseline.

3. **On American's DCA position (numerical, sourced):** American Airlines held a **~53% market share at DCA at the end of 2024** with more than 5x the route count of its nearest competitor [Source: https://simpleflying.com/american-airlines-washington-dc-routes-analysis-march-2025/]. *Use:* establishes that DCA-side standards are functionally negotiated with a single airline.

4. **On the intelligibility standard (technical, primary):** ACRP Research Report 175 identifies **STI ≥ 0.50** as the typical code-recommended minimum for public-address intelligibility in airport terminals, and documents that many US terminals do not meet it because of reverberant finishes, ambient noise, and loudspeaker geometry [Source: https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/24839/chapter/5]. *Use:* the airport industry already has a defensible primary reference for the acoustic envelope; MWAA does not need to invent one.

5. **On the airline-side operational cost of quieter terminals (direct citation):** Airlines closely track D0 performance and gate agents are increasingly motivated to close doors promptly rather than hold for stragglers [Source: https://creators.yahoo.com/lifestyle/story/they-boarded-and-left-15-minutes-early-delta-passengers-missed-flight-is-a-lesson-for-all-travelers-190958318.html]. *Use:* frames why airlines will not accept "airport eliminates the announcement, passenger misses the flight, airline pays the DBC" as an equitable division of standard-adoption cost.

